    rdfs:comment "The calendar-date primitive — the colimit object of the twin-olog diagram (prim:Date ─realization ρ→ prim:DateInt32DaysEncoding), the taiji atom of the Temporal tower. It is not two linked things; it is ONE atom glued from two facets: yin prim:formalFacet prim:Date (the civil, timezone-free whole-day type it IS) and yang prim:physicalFacet prim:DateInt32DaysEncoding (the signed INT32 days-since-epoch byte carrier it IS), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Date_Int32Days (the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow carrying the width-bounded prim:OverflowDomain effect). Because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Date — so the reversibility seal physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet is a REFLEXIVE identity that returns prim:Date exactly (spec §9d): this is a fully-sealed Date taiji, not a provisional proxy, so it carries no silm:isProvisional. prim:Date is concrete and directly realized (no transitive grounding through a descendant is needed), and this atom is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility for the Date fragment." .

# ---- (c) the colimit taiji atom — one glued primitive (formal ⊕ physical) ------------
prim:prim_DateTime a prim:Primitive ;
