    rdfs:comment "The enumeration primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:Enumeration ─realization ρ→ prim:Enumeration_Uint32Index) for the single formal type of a finite named-member set. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Enumeration (yin — a type whose values are drawn from a finite, explicitly named set, rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType, the root of the Enum tower and the parent of prim:Ordinal and prim:Categorical) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:Enumeration_Uint32Index (yang — the unsigned 32-bit member-code carrier, 32 bits / 4 bytes, descending through prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Enumeration_Uint32Index, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the exact, lossless prim:NoEffect. CONCRETE-SUPERTYPE WITNESS: prim:Enumeration is realized directly (a bare finite named set is itself instantiable, neither forced-ordered nor forced-unordered — Präriehund honesty names that fork rather than picking a side), so no descendant proxy is used and no silm:isProvisional gap is admitted. DESCENDANT SUBTYPING (spec §9a, taxonomic not grounding): prim:Ordinal and prim:Categorical are formal subtypes of prim:Enumeration, but each carries its OWN direct grounding — its own realization (prim:realize_Ordinal_Uint32Index / prim:realize_Categorical_Uint32Index) onto its own dedicated reflexive carrier (prim:Ordinal_Uint32Index / prim:Categorical_Uint32Index, each whose prim:interpretAs closes back to prim:Ordinal / prim:Categorical respectively) and its own primitive (prim:prim_Ordinal / prim:prim_Categorical). The order-preserving (Ordinal) or bare-label (Categorical) code-assignment lives on those dedicated UINT32 carriers; the ancestry to prim:Enumeration is taxonomic subtyping only, an additional §9a coverage path, NOT their grounding mechanism. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Enumeration, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Enumeration itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (NOT prim:Natural, whose UINT32 it structurally mirrors, and NOT a shared proxy carrier), and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for the finite named enumeration with NO silm:isProvisional gap because Enumeration is concrete and directly, exactly grounded on the UINT32 member-code carrier — it seeds the ordinal-ring and categorical-label structures the Atlas and glossary sub-projects build atop this Enum tower." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) The colimit Primitive atom — the glued taiji: formalFacet prim:Frame,
#     physicalFacet prim:FrameEncoding, gluedBy prim:realize_Frame.
