    prim:formalFacet prim:Frame ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:FrameEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Frame ;
    rdfs:comment "The Frame primitive — the colimit atom over the diagram (prim:Frame ─ρ→ prim:FrameEncoding), the taiji slice of the Yoneda point itself. It is ONE glued thing, not a pair of linked fields: it simultaneously IS its yin prim:formalFacet (prim:Frame, the formal Product(output,effect) type) and IS its yang prim:physicalFacet (prim:FrameEncoding, that product's byte carrier), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Frame (the Kleisli/Frame arrow carrying the typed effect). Because the gluing is a colimit it is MUTUAL: prim:FrameEncoding's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Frame, so yin holds yang and yang holds yin, and the reversibility seal physicalFacet -> interpretAs -> formalFacet returns prim:Frame EXACTLY — a TRUE IDENTITY (spec §9d), not a proxy that lands on a neighbouring type. This atom is load-bearing beyond its own row: Frame is the carrier of the realization monad by which EVERY other primitive on this floor is glued (each prim:gluedBy arrow is itself a Frame), so sealing Frame's own taiji closes the floor's self-reference — the monad's carrier is proven to be itself a fully-sealed colimit primitive. Its gluing Frame carries prim:NoEffect (faithful, lossless framing — the transported costs live in the Y coordinate, not in the framing), and it is NOT silm:isProvisional because the encoding interprets reflexively onto prim:Frame rather than onto a shared proxy carrier (contrast prim:prim_Instant / prim:prim_Decimal in taiji.ttl, whose proxies close to a different formal type). Its bytes descend prim:CompositeCarrier -> prim:Octet -> prim:Nibble -> prim:Bit, so the glued atom bottoms out at the width-1 Bit floor with no coordinate left ungrounded." .

# ---- (c) The colimit Primitive atom — the taiji (formal ⊕ physical) -----------------
prim:prim_Grapheme a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Grapheme (taiji: Grapheme ⊕ UTF-8 octet run)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Grapheme ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:GraphemeUtf8 ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Grapheme_Utf8 ;
    rdfs:comment "The grapheme-cluster primitive: the colimit object of the twin-olog diagram (prim:Grapheme ─ρ→ prim:GraphemeUtf8), one glued taiji atom that simultaneously IS its formal type (yin, prim:formalFacet prim:Grapheme) and its physical encoding (yang, prim:physicalFacet prim:GraphemeUtf8), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Grapheme_Utf8. It is not two linked fields but a single colimit thing; because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual: the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Grapheme, so the reversibility seal physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns the atom's OWN formal type — a TRUE IDENTITY round-trip (spec §9d), reflexive rather than merely non-dangling. The typed cost carried on the gluing Frame is prim:EncodingLoss (Unicode normalization sensitivity). Grapheme is a concrete Text-tower leaf realized directly through its own most-canonical carrier — the UTF-8 octet run — so this atom is fully sealed and NOT provisional, and no transitive-grounding proxy is needed. Subatomically the physical facet's octet run descends prim:byteDescendsTo Octet → Nibble → Bit to the width-1 floor, grounding the user-perceived character all the way into the byte substrate; each octet is a UTF-8 code unit and each of the cluster's codepoints occupies 1..4 such octets." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) colimit prim:Primitive atom — the taiji: ONE glued thing = formal ⊕ physical.
#     formalFacet + physicalFacet + gluedBy. The seal closes reflexively onto prim:Hash.
# =====================================================================================
prim:prim_Hash a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Hash (taiji: Hash ⊕ ByteVector(32 fixed opaque octets))" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Hash ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:HashDigestByteVector ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Hash_Digest ;
    rdfs:comment "The hash/digest primitive — the colimit-taiji atom for prim:Hash and the object this fragment exists to build, and the physical grounding SP3's S/O/P CRS consumes. It is ONE glued thing, not a linked pair: its yin prim:formalFacet prim:Hash (the fixed-width opaque digest type, rdfs:subClassOf prim:Blob in the binary/opaque tower) is glued to its yang prim:physicalFacet prim:HashDigestByteVector (the fixed 32-octet ByteVector that descends prim:ByteVector → prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 prim:Bit floor) by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Hash_Digest, the prim:NoEffect verbatim byte-identity Kleisli/Frame arrow. Because prim:HashDigestByteVector prim:interpretAs prim:Hash, the mutual-colimit round-trip physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns prim:Hash EXACTLY — a true reflexive identity (spec §9d), so the taiji is fully sealed and this atom carries NO silm:isProvisional (unlike the proxy-landing Instant/Decimal atoms of the monolithic taiji, and unlike any abstract supertype needing a descendant proxy — Hash is concrete). Hash simultaneously IS its formal digest type and IS the fixed byte vector of digest octets it realizes into; that mutual gluing (yin holds yang, yang holds yin) is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility. SP3 z-COORDINATE: the atom z is the prim:Uint16 reading of the first two of this digest's 32 octets, so the whole z geometry of the S/O/P CRS descends through this atom to the byte floor — corpus-agnostic, with no sha256 literal or corpus digest bound here." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) The colimit prim:Primitive atom — one glued taiji whose physicalFacet → interpretAs
#     returns its own formalFacet (a TRUE identity seal). No isProvisional (IRI is resolvable).
# =====================================================================================

prim:prim_IRI a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive IRI (taiji: IRI ⊕ UTF-8)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:IRI ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:IriUtf8 ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_IRI_Utf8 ;
    rdfs:comment "The internationalized-resource-identifier primitive: the colimit-taiji atom gluing yin prim:IRI to yang prim:IriUtf8 by the ρ arrow prim:realize_IRI_Utf8. Because prim:IriUtf8 prim:interpretAs prim:IRI, the mutual round-trip physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns prim:IRI EXACTLY — a TRUE reflexive identity seal (spec §9d), not a proxy that lands on the ancestor prim:URN the way the transitive prim:UrnUtf8 grounding would. SUBTYPING: IRI sits in the Identifier tower as prim:IRI rdfs:subClassOf prim:URI rdfs:subClassOf prim:URN (the spec's deliberate URN-primacy inversion) and is itself the parent of the compact-IRI prim:QName; this atom fixes UTF-8 as IRI's one canonical physical facet out of the identifier tower's shared byte substrate. PHYSICAL / EFFECT: the gluing Frame carries the prim:EncodingLoss cost of Unicode normalization and IRI↔URI percent-encoding, while the byte substrate descends prim:ByteVector → prim:Octet → prim:Bit so the atom bottoms out at the width-1 floor. It is a fully-sealed taiji requiring NO silm:isProvisional — IRI is a resolvable, concrete identifier type, so the PROVISIONAL-dodge reserved for genuinely undecidable gaps is forbidden here (spec §9b)." .

# ---- (c) The colimit prim:Primitive atom: Imaginary ⊕ ImaginaryFloat64Encoding, glued by ρ -------
# The taiji: Imaginary (yin) ⊕ ImaginaryFloat64Encoding (yang), glued by the ρ above. The physical
# facet's interpretAs closes back onto prim:Imaginary, so the seal is a reflexive TRUE IDENTITY.
prim:ImaginaryPrimitive a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Imaginary (colimit taiji: Imaginary ⊕ IEEE-754 double imaginary axis)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Imaginary ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:ImaginaryFloat64Encoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:ImaginaryRealizesFloat64 ;
    rdfs:comment "The imaginary-number primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:Imaginary ─realization ρ→ prim:ImaginaryFloat64Encoding) for the single formal type of the imaginary axis. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Imaginary (yin — the real multiples of the imaginary unit i where i² = −1, the facet of prim:Complex with zero real part, sitting prim:Imaginary ⊂ prim:Complex and deliberately NOT ⊂ prim:Real) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:ImaginaryFloat64Encoding (yang — the single IEEE-754 Float64 imaginary-coordinate carrier, 64 bits / 8 bytes, descending through prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:ImaginaryRealizesFloat64, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the finite-grid prim:RoundingIEEE754 effect. JOIN WITNESS: because the imaginary axis reuses the SAME IEEE-754 double machine type as the real axis, distinguished only by its prim:interpretAs target, this primitive is the physical witness that the number-tower top prim:Complex is the JOIN of a real axis (prim:Real) and an imaginary axis (prim:Imaginary) — the imaginary member of the Cartesian complex product prim:ProductComplexFloat64 is exactly this encoding. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Imaginary, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Imaginary itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (NOT prim:Real, whose Float64 it structurally mirrors), and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for the imaginary axis with NO silm:isProvisional gap because Imaginary is concrete and directly, exactly grounded on the Real-axis double carrier — the imaginary facet that completes the what-is-a-number litmus at the top of the ℕ⊂ℤ⊂ℚ⊂ℝ⊂ℂ chain." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) The colimit Primitive atom for prim:Instant — the glued taiji (formal ⊕ physical).
#     ONE atom that simultaneously IS prim:Instant (yin) and IS the epoch encoding (yang),
#     glued by the realization ρ above. Reflexive round-trip:
#         physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet
#       = prim:InstantInt64Epoch → prim:Instant → prim:Instant   (TRUE IDENTITY).
# =====================================================================================

prim:primitive_Instant a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Instant (colimit taiji: Instant ⊕ INT64 epoch tick)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Instant ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:InstantInt64Epoch ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Instant_Epoch ;
    rdfs:comment "The time-line-instant primitive — the colimit object of the twin-olog diagram (prim:Instant ─realization ρ→ prim:InstantInt64Epoch) for the single formal type Instant. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Instant (yin — an absolute point on the continuous time line, rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType, the Temporal tower's clock-reading independent of calendar or timezone, distinct from Duration/Interval/DateTime) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:InstantInt64Epoch (yang — the signed 64-bit two's-complement little-endian epoch-tick word descending through prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Instant_Epoch, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the temporal-quantization prim:EpochPrecision effect. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Instant, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Instant itself, a TRUE IDENTITY, and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. This is the source-level fix for the panel-flagged non-reflexive Instant → INT64 → Integer round-trip (the superseded provisional prim:prim_Instant glued Instant to the shared prim:Int64 whose interpretAs is prim:Integer): yin holds yang and yang holds yin, the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split ↔ consolidated render reversibility, a fully-sealed taiji carrying NO silm:isProvisional marker because Instant is resolvably and completely grounded on its dedicated epoch-tick carrier this iteration." .

# ---- (c) the colimit prim:Primitive atom (one glued atom = ℤ ⊕ INT64) --------------
# The taiji: Integer (yin) ⊕ IntegerCanonicalEncoding (yang), glued by the ρ above. The
# physical facet's interpretAs closes back onto prim:Integer, so the seal is reflexive.
prim:primitive_Integer a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive ℤ (colimit taiji: Integer ⊕ INT64)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Integer ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:IntegerCanonicalEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Integer_Canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "The integer primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:Integer ─realization ρ→ prim:IntegerCanonicalEncoding) for the single formal type ℤ. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Integer (yin — the whole numbers with sign, rdfs:subClassOf prim:Rational, superclass of prim:Natural and prim:Bignum) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:IntegerCanonicalEncoding (yang — the signed 64-bit two's-complement little-endian word descending through prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Integer_Canonical, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the width-bounded prim:OverflowDomain effect. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Integer, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Integer itself, a TRUE IDENTITY, and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for ℤ with no silm:isProvisional gap because Integer is directly and losslessly grounded on the signed fixed-width machine carrier." .

# ---- (c) colimit taiji atom — one glued primitive, physicalFacet→interpretAs=formalFacet
prim:prim_Interval a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Interval (taiji: Interval ⊕ Product(INT64 start, INT64 end))" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Interval ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:IntervalProductInstantPair ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Interval_InstantPair ;
    rdfs:comment "The anchored-time-span primitive — the colimit object of the twin-olog diagram (prim:Interval ─realization ρ→ prim:IntervalProductInstantPair), ONE glued taiji atom, not two linked fields. Its yin prim:formalFacet is prim:Interval (the mathematical anchored-span type it IS, an rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType and the anchored sibling of Duration) and its yang prim:physicalFacet is prim:IntervalProductInstantPair (the two-INT64-epoch product carrier it IS); they are glued by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Interval_InstantPair, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow whose prim:realizesFrom is this formalFacet and whose prim:frameOutput is this physicalFacet, carrying the width-bounded prim:OverflowDomain cost. SEAL: because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Interval, so the reversibility round-trip physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns prim:Interval itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (spec §9d), making this a fully-sealed taiji. It is deliberately NOT silm:isProvisional: Interval is concrete and resolvable, realized directly rather than through a descendant or a shared proxy carrier (spec §9a/§9b), so unlike the provisional Instant/Decimal proxy atoms in taiji.ttl this atom's seal closes reflexively onto its own formal type." .

# ---- (c) the colimit taiji atom: the glued Kleene3 primitive ------------------------
# The one glued thing that simultaneously IS prim:Kleene3 (yin) and IS prim:Kleene3Uint8Code
# (yang), joined by prim:realize_Kleene3_Uint8Code. Because the gluing is a colimit it is
# mutual: the physical facet's prim:interpretAs closes back to prim:Kleene3, so
# physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns prim:Kleene3 exactly — a TRUE IDENTITY.
prim:prim_Kleene3_Uint8Code a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Kleene3 (taiji: Kleene3 ⊕ UINT8(0/1/2))" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Kleene3 ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:Kleene3Uint8Code ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Kleene3_Uint8Code ;
    rdfs:comment "The three-valued-logic primitive as the colimit object of the twin-olog diagram (FormalType ─realization ρ→ PhysicalEncoding) — one glued taiji atom, not a pair of linked fields. It simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:Kleene3 (yin — three-valued Kleene logic over true/false/unknown, a direct subclass of prim:FormalType and the SUPERTYPE of prim:Bool, since Boolean logic is Kleene logic with the unknown value forbidden) and IS its physical facet prim:Kleene3Uint8Code (yang — the UINT8(0/1/2) one-octet three-valued code cell), joined by the gluing morphism prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Kleene3_Uint8Code (the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow carrying prim:NoEffect). Because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual: the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Kleene3, so the reversibility seal physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns prim:Kleene3 exactly — a true reflexive identity and a fully-sealed taiji, not a provisional proxy that would land on a different formal type (contrast the deliberately-narrower prim:Bool primitive, which seals onto Bool, and the temporal/decimal proxies that seal onto Integer/Codepoint). prim:Kleene3 is a concrete, resolvable type — a supertype but not an abstract or uninhabited one — so this atom is realized directly with no isProvisional dodge and no transitive-grounding indirection. The load-bearing physical fact of the tower is captured here: unlike prim:Bool, whose two values can ride a single prim:Bit, Kleene3's three values need at least two bits (ceil(log2 3) = 2), so its sealed grounding byte-descends the whole octet prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 prim:Bit floor, the base unit of the whole primitive floor, with the packed 2-bit trit as its tightest sub-octet sibling." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) The COLIMIT PRIMITIVE atom — the glued taiji: Latitude ⊕ LatitudeFloat64
# =====================================================================================
prim:prim_Latitude a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Latitude (taiji: Latitude ⊕ Float64 degrees)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Latitude ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:LatitudeFloat64 ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Latitude_Float64 ;
    rdfs:comment "The latitude primitive — the colimit object of the twin-olog diagram (prim:Latitude ─realization ρ→ prim:LatitudeFloat64), one glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal type (yin prim:formalFacet prim:Latitude) and IS its physical encoding (yang prim:physicalFacet prim:LatitudeFloat64), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Latitude_Float64 (the Kleisli/Frame arrow carrying the prim:RoundingIEEE754 effect). Because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual and, here, reflexive: prim:LatitudeFloat64 prim:interpretAs prim:Latitude, so the reversibility seal physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns this atom's own formal facet prim:Latitude — a TRUE identity round-trip, not the near-miss onto the supertype prim:Coordinate that the ancestral prim:CoordinateFloat64 grounding would give. This is a fully-sealed taiji in the geospatial tower, the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility: yin holds yang and yang holds yin over a scalar 8-octet IEEE-754 double whose descent bottoms at the prim:Bit floor. It satisfies the SHACL PrimitiveShape (all three coordinates present) and carries no provisional marking (spec §9d)." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) The colimit prim:Primitive atom — one glued taiji object (Line ⊕ LineWkbGeometry).
#     physicalFacet → interpretAs == formalFacet == prim:Line: a fully-sealed identity.
# =====================================================================================
prim:prim_Line a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Line (taiji: Line ⊕ WKB linestring geometry)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Line ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:LineWkbGeometry ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Line_WkbGeometry ;
    rdfs:comment "The line-geometry primitive — the colimit-taiji atom for the geospatial tower's one-dimensional geometry: yin prim:Line glued to yang prim:LineWkbGeometry by the ρ arrow prim:realize_Line_WkbGeometry (prim:RoundingIEEE754 effect). It is ONE glued colimit object, not a loose pair of links: it simultaneously IS the formal Line type and IS its WKB byte encoding, joined by the gluing morphism named in prim:gluedBy whose prim:realizesFrom is this formal facet and whose prim:encoding is this physical facet. Because prim:LineWkbGeometry prim:interpretAs prim:Line, the mutual round-trip physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns prim:Line exactly — a TRUE IDENTITY seal (reflexive per spec §9d), the fully-closed taiji with no proxy carrier and no provisional gap, unlike the Instant/Decimal proxy atoms whose interpretAs lands on a different formal type. COMPOSITE-OVER-POINT WITNESS: a Line is an ordered run of two-or-more prim:Point vertices, and its physical facet reuses the Point coordinate payload — a Product(Float64 X, Float64 Y) — once per vertex, so this primitive sits one dimension above prim:prim_Point in the tower and one below the Polygon that closes such a run into a ring; its formal facet is concrete (Line ⊂ FormalType, self-realized, needing no transitive-grounding indirection through an ancestor or descendant). Its physical facet descends octet-by-octet — via prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit — to the width-1 prim:Bit floor, so the primitive is grounded continuously from the mathematics of a polyline all the way down to the bit substrate; downstream it is the one-dimensional geometry the S/O/P-tower CRS sub-project and GeoSPARQL build on." .

# ---- (c) The colimit prim:Primitive atom: List ⊕ ListSequenceEncoding, glued by ρ ---------------
# The taiji: List (yin) ⊕ ListSequenceEncoding (yang), glued by the ρ above. The physical facet's
# interpretAs closes back onto prim:List, so the seal is a reflexive TRUE IDENTITY.
prim:ListPrimitive a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive List (colimit taiji: List ⊕ length-prefixed homogeneous run)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:List ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:ListSequenceEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:ListRealizesSequence ;
    rdfs:comment "The list / sequence primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:List ─realization ρ→ prim:ListSequenceEncoding) for the single formal type List. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:List (yin — the ordered, variable-length, homogeneous sequence, rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType at the head of the Aggregate tower's ordered-sequence branch, the parent of the fixed-length prim:Vector and the ordered counterpart of the unordered prim:Set and prim:Bag) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:ListSequenceEncoding (yang — the length-prefixed homogeneous run of the member encodings over the prim:ByteVector ordered-byte-vector carrier, a UINT32 count prefix plus that many contiguous element encodings, octet-granular and little-endian, descending through prim:ByteVector → prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:ListRealizesSequence, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the lossless-framing prim:NoEffect. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:List, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:List itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (it lands on List, not on its prim:Vector subtype nor a bare prim:ByteVector), and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for the ordered sequence with NO silm:isProvisional gap because List is concrete and directly, exactly grounded on the length-prefixed-run-over-ByteVector carrier — the length-prefixed sequence atom the AOB tensor/aggregate block and every ordered-collection formal type of the floor grounds its member layout into." .

# ---- (c) The colimit primitive atom (the glued taiji object) -------------------------
# The taiji: prim:prim_Literal is the colimit object over (prim:Literal ─ρ→ prim:LiteralUtf8Datatype).
# It is ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal type (formalFacet) and IS its physical
# encoding (physicalFacet), joined by prim:gluedBy (the ρ arrow above). Reflexive seal (§9d):
#   physicalFacet(prim_Literal) = prim:LiteralUtf8Datatype
#   prim:LiteralUtf8Datatype prim:interpretAs prim:Literal
#   formalFacet(prim_Literal)   = prim:Literal
#   ⇒ physicalFacet → interpretAs == formalFacet   (TRUE identity, no proxy).
prim:prim_Literal a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Literal (taiji: Literal ⊕ UTF-8 lexical+datatype)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Literal ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:LiteralUtf8Datatype ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Literal_Utf8Datatype ;
    rdfs:comment "The RDF-literal primitive — the colimit object of the twin-olog diagram (prim:Literal ─ρ→ prim:LiteralUtf8Datatype), the taiji atom for the RDF-term tower's typed/lang-tagged literal. It is not two linked things: it is ONE atom glued from yin prim:Literal (its formalFacet, the mathematical/logical term it IS) and yang prim:LiteralUtf8Datatype (its physicalFacet, the octet-granular UTF-8 lexical+datatype byte-carrier it IS), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Literal_Utf8Datatype (the Kleisli/Frame arrow carrying the prim:EncodingLoss cost of the gluing). Because the gluing is a colimit it is MUTUAL and the seal is a TRUE reflexive identity: the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Literal, the very same type as the formal facet, so physicalFacet → interpretAs == formalFacet returns Literal itself — not a proxy such as Codepoint or URN. Subatomically the atom bottoms out at the width-1 prim:Bit floor through prim:ByteVector → prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit, and its two member coordinates (a UTF-8 codepoint stream for the lexical form, a URN for the datatype/language tag) are themselves realized carriers; its distinctive dual nature is that, via that datatype URN, it also grounds transitively into the Number, Text, or Temporal tower it denotes. This mutual-colimit round-trip is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility." .

# ---- (c) colimit Primitive atom — glues yin (formal) and yang (physical) -------------
prim:prim_Longitude a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Longitude (taiji: Longitude ⊕ Float64 degrees)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Longitude ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:LongitudeFloat64 ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Longitude_Float64 ;
    rdfs:comment "The east-west-longitude primitive: the colimit-taiji atom over the small diagram (prim:Longitude ─ρ→ prim:LongitudeFloat64), gluing yin prim:Longitude (prim:formalFacet — the geographic east-west angular type it IS) to yang prim:LongitudeFloat64 (prim:physicalFacet — the 8-byte little-endian IEEE-754 double carrier it IS) by the ρ arrow prim:realize_Longitude_Float64 (prim:gluedBy), which carries the prim:RoundingIEEE754 effect on its gluing Frame. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom: because prim:LongitudeFloat64 prim:interpretAs prim:Longitude, the mutual round-trip physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns prim:Longitude exactly — a TRUE reflexive identity seal (spec §9d), where the ancestral generic prim:Coordinate grounding would have closed non-reflexively onto Coordinate instead. This is a fully-sealed, NON-provisional taiji (no silm:isProvisional): the atom simultaneously is the longitude type and is its double carrier, and that carrier descends subatomically through eight prim:Octet carriers to the width-1 prim:Bit floor, so yin holds yang and yang holds yin all the way down to the byte substrate. Longitude is additionally grounded transitively through its realized ancestor prim:Coordinate (prim:realize_Coordinate_Float64 / prim:CoordinateFloat64) — an ancestral grounding STEP B now MATERIALISES as the real edge prim:agp_Longitude_Coordinate (prim:ancestralViaArrow prim:sub_Longitude_Coordinate, prim:ancestralViaTransport prim:rt_sub_Longitude_Coordinate, prim:ancestralLandsIn prim:CoordinateFloat64Encoding = rho(prim:Coordinate)), so the once-prose 'also grounded through the ancestor' is now a resolvable graph fact, so both the direct and the ancestral dual-grounding paths of spec §9a hold; the direct path is the canonical one this Primitive commits to." .

# ---- (c) The colimit prim:Primitive atom: Map ⊕ MapAssociativeEncoding, glued by ρ --------------
# The taiji: Map (yin) ⊕ MapAssociativeEncoding (yang), glued by the ρ above. The physical facet's
# interpretAs closes back onto prim:Map, so the seal is a reflexive TRUE IDENTITY.
prim:MapPrimitive a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Map (colimit taiji: Map ⊕ canonically key-sorted length-prefixed key-value pair run)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Map ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:MapAssociativeEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:MapRealizesAssociative ;
    rdfs:comment "The map / dictionary / associative-array primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:Map ─realization ρ→ prim:MapAssociativeEncoding) for the single formal type Map, the taiji atom taiji.ttl did not previously carry for Map. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Map (yin — the finite partial function from a key type to a value type on unique keys, rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType in the Aggregate tower, viewable as a prim:Set of key·value prim:Tuple pairs under a key-uniqueness constraint but kept its own object for its functional-lookup semantics, and the associative counterpart of the plain unordered prim:Set / prim:Bag and the ordered prim:List) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:MapAssociativeEncoding (yang — the canonically key-sorted, length-prefixed run of the (key, value) encoding pairs over the prim:ByteVector ordered-byte-vector carrier, a UINT32 entry-count prefix plus that many contiguous unique-keyed key·value prim:CompositeCarrier products in canonical key order, octet-granular and little-endian, descending through prim:ByteVector / prim:CompositeCarrier → prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:MapRealizesAssociative, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the prim:OrderingCanonicalization effect (the canonical key sort a map incurs because its entries have no intrinsic order). REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Map, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Map itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (it lands on Map, not on a prim:Set of pairs nor a bare prim:ByteVector), and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for the associative map with NO silm:isProvisional gap because Map is concrete and directly, exactly grounded on the key-sorted-kv-run-over-ByteVector carrier — the canonical key-value atom every associative formal type of the floor grounds its key·value entry layout into." .

# ---- (c) The colimit prim:Primitive atom: Measurement ⊕ MeasurementProductEncoding, glued by ρ ----
# The taiji: Measurement (yin) ⊕ MeasurementProductEncoding (yang), glued by the ρ above. The
# physical facet's interpretAs closes back onto prim:Measurement, so the seal is a reflexive TRUE
# IDENTITY.
prim:MeasurementPrimitive a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Measurement (colimit taiji: Measurement ⊕ Product(Float64 value, Float64 uncertainty))" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Measurement ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:MeasurementProductEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:MeasurementRealizesProduct ;
    rdfs:comment "The measurement primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:Measurement ─realization ρ→ prim:MeasurementProductEncoding) for the single formal type Measurement. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Measurement (yin — a Quantity enriched with an uncertainty, a direct subclass of prim:Quantity: where a bare Quantity asserts an exact magnitude, a Measurement admits its own imprecision, so empirical values with error bars live here) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:MeasurementProductEncoding (yang — the value·uncertainty product of two IEEE-754 Float64 members over the prim:CompositeCarrier product carrier, total 128 bits / 16 bytes, each member interpreting to prim:Real, descending through prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:MeasurementRealizesProduct, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the finite-grid prim:RoundingIEEE754 effect on both coordinates. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Measurement, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Measurement itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (it lands on Measurement, not on its parent prim:Quantity nor on the prim:Real of a single member), and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for Measurement with NO silm:isProvisional gap because Measurement is concrete and directly, exactly grounded on the pair-of-doubles carrier — a value made honest by carrying the dispersion of its own imprecision, grounded recursively through its member encodings to the byte substrate." .

# ---- (c) the colimit prim:Primitive atom (one glued atom = ℕ ⊕ UINT64) --------------
# The taiji: Natural (yin) ⊕ NaturalCanonicalEncoding (yang), glued by the ρ above. The
# physical facet's interpretAs closes back onto prim:Natural, so the seal is reflexive.
prim:primitive_Natural a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive ℕ (colimit taiji: Natural ⊕ UINT64)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Natural ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:NaturalCanonicalEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Natural_Canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "The natural-number primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:Natural ─realization ρ→ prim:NaturalCanonicalEncoding) for the single formal type ℕ. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Natural (yin — the non-negative counting floor of the number tower, rdfs:subClassOf prim:Integer, with the zero-inclusion fork resolved by its named sub-objects prim:NaturalWithZero and prim:NaturalWithoutZero) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:NaturalCanonicalEncoding (yang — the unsigned 64-bit little-endian word descending through prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Natural_Canonical, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the width-bounded prim:OverflowDomain effect. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Natural, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Natural itself, a TRUE IDENTITY, and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for ℕ with NO silm:isProvisional gap because Natural is directly and losslessly grounded on the unsigned fixed-width machine carrier — the distinction from its signed supertype ℤ being carried entirely by prim:signedness prim:Unsigned." .

# ---- (c) the colimit prim:Primitive atom (one glued atom = ℕ₀ ⊕ UINT8) --------------
# The taiji: NaturalWithZero (yin) ⊕ NaturalWithZeroCanonicalEncoding (yang), glued by the ρ
# above. The physical facet's interpretAs closes back onto prim:NaturalWithZero, so the seal
# is reflexive — a TRUE IDENTITY, the property the task's roundtrip_identity check asserts.
prim:primitive_NaturalWithZero a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive ℕ₀ (colimit taiji: NaturalWithZero ⊕ UINT8)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:NaturalWithZero ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:NaturalWithZeroCanonicalEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_NaturalWithZero_Canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "The natural-with-zero primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:NaturalWithZero ─realization ρ→ prim:NaturalWithZeroCanonicalEncoding) for the single formal type ℕ₀ = {0, 1, 2, ...}. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:NaturalWithZero (yin — the 0-inclusive reading of the natural numbers, rdfs:subClassOf prim:Natural, the named sub-object that resolves the zero-inclusion fork in favour of admitting 0, its complement being prim:NaturalWithoutZero) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:NaturalWithZeroCanonicalEncoding (yang — the unsigned single-octet UINT8 whose ordinal floor 0 offset-freely carries the counting value, descending through prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_NaturalWithZero_Canonical, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the width-bounded prim:OverflowDomain effect. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:NaturalWithZero, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:NaturalWithZero itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (not merely onto its supertype ℕ, which is what the inherited ancestor encodings would yield), and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for ℕ₀ with NO silm:isProvisional gap because NaturalWithZero is directly and losslessly grounded on the unsigned fixed-width machine carrier — the 0-inclusiveness being carried by the unsigned code space's ordinal floor 0, and the whole sub-tower's distinction from the signed supertype ℤ being carried by prim:signedness prim:Unsigned." .

# ---- (c) The colimit-taiji primitive atom — formal ⊕ physical, fully sealed ----------
prim:prim_NaturalWithoutZero a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive ℕ⁺ (taiji: NaturalWithoutZero ⊕ UINT32 ordinal-floor-1)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:NaturalWithoutZero ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:NaturalWithoutZeroUint32 ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_NaturalWithoutZero_Uint32 ;
    rdfs:comment "The strictly-positive-natural primitive — the colimit object of the twin-olog diagram (prim:NaturalWithoutZero ─realization ρ→ prim:NaturalWithoutZeroUint32), one glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal type (yin: ℕ⁺ = {1,2,3,...}, a direct subclass of prim:Natural and thereby of prim:Integer/prim:Rational/prim:Real/prim:Complex up the number tower) and IS its physical encoding (yang: an unsigned 32-bit carrier whose ordinal floor is 1, four octets descending Octet→Nibble→Bit to the width-1 floor). The two facets are joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_NaturalWithoutZero_Uint32, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow whose typed cost is the width-bounded prim:OverflowDomain effect. Because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual: the physical facet's prim:interpretAs closes back onto prim:NaturalWithoutZero, so the reversibility seal physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet is a TRUE reflexive identity (spec §9d) — this taiji is fully sealed, with no shared-carrier proxy and no silm:isProvisional. It is the sibling of prim:prim_Natural in the number tower, differing solely in that the value 0 is excluded from its ordinal domain, the honest fork the formal tower names rather than silently picking a zero-convention (Präriehund honesty)." .

# ---- (c) The colimit prim:Primitive atom: Optional ⊕ OptionalPresenceEncoding, glued by ρ --------
# The taiji: Optional (yin) ⊕ OptionalPresenceEncoding (yang), glued by the ρ above. The physical
# facet's interpretAs closes back onto prim:Optional, so the seal is a reflexive TRUE IDENTITY.
prim:OptionalPrimitive a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Optional (colimit taiji: Optional ⊕ presence tag + optional payload)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Optional ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:OptionalPresenceEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:OptionalRealizesPresence ;
    rdfs:comment "The optional / maybe primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:Optional ─realization ρ→ prim:OptionalPresenceEncoding) for the single formal type Optional. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Optional (yin — the two-alternative tagged union none | some(value), the coproduct Sum(Unit, T), rdfs:subClassOf prim:Sum in the Algebraic-constructor tower and the structural representation of nullability kept distinct from the three-valued prim:Kleene3) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:OptionalPresenceEncoding (yang — the presence-tag-plus-optional-payload frame over the prim:ByteVector ordered-byte-vector carrier, a UINT8 tag 0=none/1=some followed when present by the wrapped type's member encoding, octet-granular and little-endian, descending through prim:ByteVector → prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:OptionalRealizesPresence, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the lossless-framing prim:NoEffect. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Optional, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Optional itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (it lands on Optional, not on its prim:Sum supertype nor a bare prim:ByteVector), and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split ↔ consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for the option type with NO silm:isProvisional gap because Optional is concrete and directly, exactly grounded on the presence-tag-plus-payload-over-ByteVector carrier — the maybe atom that the projection packet's loss classes and every nullable field of the floor grounds its absent/present structure into." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) The colimit primitive atom — Ordinal glued to its order-preserving code (TRUE IDENTITY).
# =====================================================================================
# The taiji: Ordinal (yin) ⊕ Ordinal_Uint32Index (yang), glued by the ρ above. The physical
# facet's interpretAs closes back onto prim:Ordinal, so the seal is a reflexive TRUE IDENTITY.
prim:prim_Ordinal a prim:Primitive ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive Ordinal (colimit taiji: Ordinal ⊕ UINT32 order-preserving member code)" ;
    prim:formalFacet prim:Ordinal ;
    prim:physicalFacet prim:Ordinal_Uint32Index ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Ordinal_Uint32Index ;
    rdfs:comment "The ordinal primitive — the colimit object over the twin-olog diagram (prim:Ordinal ─realization ρ→ prim:Ordinal_Uint32Index) for the single formal type of an ordered finite named-member set. It is not two linked things but ONE glued atom that simultaneously IS its formal facet prim:formalFacet prim:Ordinal (yin — a finite named set carrying a total order, rdfs:subClassOf prim:Enumeration rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType, the ordered sibling of prim:Categorical, home of low<medium<high and the ordered positions of the 21-column Atlas ring) and IS its physical facet prim:physicalFacet prim:Ordinal_Uint32Index (yang — the order-preserving unsigned 32-bit rank-code carrier, 32 bits / 4 bytes, descending through prim:Octet → prim:Nibble → prim:Bit to the width-1 floor), joined by prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Ordinal_Uint32Index, the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow that carries the yin into the yang bearing the exact, lossless prim:NoEffect. CONCRETE-LEAF WITNESS: prim:Ordinal is a concrete, directly-realizable leaf of the Enum tower (it has no subclasses), realized directly here rather than through any descendant proxy, so no silm:isProvisional gap is admitted (spec §9b/§9d). TRANSITIVE-GROUNDING LINK (spec §9a): prim:Ordinal is additionally covered by ancestry through its realized supertype prim:Enumeration (whose prim:Enumeration_Uint32Index grounds every enumeration, ordinal included, by inheritance) — this primitive SUPERSEDES that ancestral cover with a direct, reflexive grounding so the order-preservation invariant survives into the seal rather than dissolving into the generic parent index. REFLEXIVE SEAL (spec §9d): because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Ordinal, so the round-trip prim:physicalFacet → prim:interpretAs → prim:formalFacet returns prim:Ordinal itself, a TRUE IDENTITY (NOT prim:Natural, whose UINT32 it structurally mirrors, NOT the supertype prim:Enumeration, and NOT a shared proxy carrier), and the full reversibility loop physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet → realizesAs → encoding returns the chosen encoding. yin holds yang and yang holds yin; this is the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility, sealed here for the ordered finite enumeration with NO silm:isProvisional gap because Ordinal is concrete and directly, exactly grounded on the order-preserving UINT32 rank-code carrier — it seeds the ordinal-ring structures the Atlas and glossary sub-projects build atop this Enum tower. It satisfies the SHACL PrimitiveShape (all three coordinates present) and carries no provisional marking." .

# =====================================================================================
# (c) The colimit prim:Primitive atom — one glued taiji object (Point ⊕ PointWkbGeometry).
#     physicalFacet → interpretAs == formalFacet == prim:Point: a fully-sealed identity.
