    prim:physicalFacet prim:PolygonWkbEncoding ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_Polygon_WkbFrame ;
    rdfs:comment "The polygon primitive — the colimit-taiji atom that simultaneously IS the formal geometry prim:Polygon (yin, prim:formalFacet) and its Well-Known-Binary byte encoding prim:PolygonWkbEncoding (yang, prim:physicalFacet), glued by the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow prim:realize_Polygon_WkbFrame (prim:gluedBy) carrying the IEEE-754 rounding effect of its embedded Float64 coordinates. It is ONE glued object, not a loose pair of fields: because the gluing is a colimit it is mutual — the physical facet's prim:interpretAs points back to prim:Polygon, so the reversibility seal physicalFacet -> interpretAs -> formalFacet returns prim:Polygon exactly, a TRUE identity round-trip (spec §9d), the per-primitive instance of the unary law's split↔consolidated render reversibility. This fully-sealed atom grounds the Geospatial tower's two-dimensional area geometry into the byte substrate — descending prim:ByteVector -> prim:Octet -> prim:Nibble -> prim:Bit — and seeds the GeoSPARQL and S/O/P-tower CRS consumers; corpus-agnostic, pure shape, no live-corpus binding (that is W5)." .

# ---- (c) Colimit Primitive atom — the fully-sealed reflexive taiji ----------------------
prim:prim_QName a prim:Primitive ;
