    prim:physicalFacet prim:QNameUtf8 ;
    prim:gluedBy prim:realize_QName_Utf8 ;
    rdfs:comment "The qualified-name primitive: the colimit-taiji atom gluing yin prim:QName (the compact-IRI / CURIE leaf of the identifier tower QName ⊂ IRI ⊂ URI ⊂ URN) to yang prim:QNameUtf8 (its interpreted UTF-8 octet carrier) by the ρ Kleisli/Frame arrow prim:gluedBy prim:realize_QName_Utf8. It is not two linked things but one glued atom: the atom simultaneously IS its formal type and IS its byte encoding. Because prim:QNameUtf8 prim:interpretAs prim:QName, the mutual round-trip physicalFacet → interpretAs → formalFacet returns prim:QName EXACTLY — a fully-sealed, reflexive taiji (a TRUE identity, spec §9d), not a proxy grounding onto an ancestor as the earlier Instant/Decimal proxies were. It is NOT provisional: QName is a resolvable concrete type carrying its own direct realization, so no silm:isProvisional dodge applies (spec §9b). The gluing Frame carries prim:EncodingLoss (UTF-8 surrogate/normalization plus the out-of-band prefix-map dependency of CURIE expansion); the physical facet descends subatomically octet → nibble → bit to the width-1 prim:Bit floor, so nothing escapes the byte substrate. QName is additionally grounded by ancestry through prim:URN's realization (spec §9a transitive grounding); this atom records the tighter DIRECT self-realization whose encoding interprets back to QName rather than to URN." .

