# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# yo on arrows + rho naturality square — one per SubtypeArrow generator (59 arrows).
# Each square: top yo(f): yo(A)->yo(B); bottom rho(f)=RealizationTransport: rho(A)->rho(B);
# left rho_A; right rho_B. Commutes because the thin category has a unique arrow per pair.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
prim:yo_sub_Bag_FormalType a prim:YonedaArrow ; prim:yonedaArrowOf prim:sub_Bag_FormalType ; prim:yonedaArrowDom prim:repr_Bag ; prim:yonedaArrowCod prim:repr_FormalType ;
    rdfs:label "yo(sub_Bag_FormalType): Hom(-, prim:Bag) -> Hom(-, prim:FormalType)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The image under the Yoneda embedding yo of the subtype arrow prim:sub_Bag_FormalType (prim:Bag sub prim:FormalType): a natural transformation yo(prim:sub_Bag_FormalType): yo(prim:Bag) = prim:repr_Bag -> yo(prim:FormalType) = prim:repr_FormalType between the two representable presheaves, given by post-composition with prim:sub_Bag_FormalType (a member g: X -> prim:Bag of Hom(X, prim:Bag) is sent to prim:sub_Bag_FormalType after g: X -> prim:FormalType in Hom(X, prim:FormalType)). prim:yonedaArrowOf records that it is the yo-image of exactly the one arrow prim:sub_Bag_FormalType; because the formal category is thin, the assignment (arrow prim:Bag -> prim:FormalType) <-> (natural transformation yo(prim:Bag) -> yo(prim:FormalType)) is a BIJECTION Hom(prim:Bag, prim:FormalType) ~ Nat(yo(prim:Bag), yo(prim:FormalType)), the checkable finite form of Yoneda fullness. It is the top edge of the naturality square prim:natsq_sub_Bag_FormalType, opposite the transported carrier arrow rho(prim:sub_Bag_FormalType) = prim:rt_sub_Bag_FormalType." .
prim:natsq_sub_Bag_FormalType a prim:NaturalitySquare ; prim:natOfArrow prim:sub_Bag_FormalType ; prim:natYonedaArrow prim:yo_sub_Bag_FormalType ; prim:natComponentDom prim:rhoNat_Bag ; prim:natTransport prim:rt_sub_Bag_FormalType ; prim:natComponentCod prim:rhoNat_FormalType ; prim:natCommutes true ;
    rdfs:label "naturality square of rho over sub_Bag_FormalType" ;
    rdfs:comment "The naturality square witnessing that rho: yo => R is natural over the subtype arrow prim:sub_Bag_FormalType (prim:Bag sub prim:FormalType). Its four edges are genuine, resolvable morphisms: TOP prim:natYonedaArrow prim:yo_sub_Bag_FormalType = yo(prim:sub_Bag_FormalType): yo(prim:Bag) prim:repr_Bag -> yo(prim:FormalType) prim:repr_FormalType; BOTTOM prim:natTransport prim:rt_sub_Bag_FormalType = rho(prim:sub_Bag_FormalType): rho(prim:Bag) prim:BagMultisetEncoding -> rho(prim:FormalType) prim:ByteVector (the STEP B RealizationTransport, whose transportDom/transportCod are pinned to rhoObject of the arrow's domain and codomain); LEFT prim:natComponentDom prim:rhoNat_Bag: yo(prim:Bag) -> rho(prim:Bag); RIGHT prim:natComponentCod prim:rhoNat_FormalType: yo(prim:FormalType) -> rho(prim:FormalType). The square commutes (prim:natCommutes true): both composite paths yo(prim:Bag) -> rho(prim:FormalType) — down-then-across (rho_Bag then rho(prim:sub_Bag_FormalType)) and across-then-down (yo(prim:sub_Bag_FormalType) then rho_FormalType) — share corners yo(prim:Bag) and rho(prim:FormalType), and because the thin category and its physical-carrier image each carry at most one arrow per ordered pair, the two paths are the SAME arrow. Corner agreement is teeth-checkable: yonedaArrowDom(top)=rhoComponentSource(left)=prim:repr_Bag, yonedaArrowCod(top)=rhoComponentSource(right)=prim:repr_FormalType, transportDom(bottom)=rhoComponentTarget(left)=prim:BagMultisetEncoding, transportCod(bottom)=rhoComponentTarget(right)=prim:ByteVector." .

prim:yo_sub_Bignum_Integer a prim:YonedaArrow ; prim:yonedaArrowOf prim:sub_Bignum_Integer ; prim:yonedaArrowDom prim:repr_Bignum ; prim:yonedaArrowCod prim:repr_Integer ;
    rdfs:label "yo(sub_Bignum_Integer): Hom(-, prim:Bignum) -> Hom(-, prim:Integer)" ;
