# The presheaf olog (olog-of-ologs) meta-object + the unary-law Yoneda-point tie
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
prim:presheafOlog a prim:PresheafOlog , prim:OlogObject ;
    rdfs:label "PSh(FormalOlog) — the olog of ologs" ;
    rdfs:comment "The presheaf olog PSh(FormalOlog): the category of Set-valued presheaves on the thin formal olog, into which the Yoneda embedding yo lands the formal olog and among whose objects the representables prim:repr_<A> = Hom(-, A) sit as the yo-image. A presheaf is itself an olog (a Set-valued diagram), so every object of this category is an olog — hence prim:presheafOlog a prim:OlogObject too: being itself an olog, the presheaf olog is an object of the next meta-olog up, and the construction recurses without end, Directive 2's ologs of ologs, turtles all the way down. It is honestly NOT asserted to be a member of itself (that would be an object of PSh(PSh(FormalOlog)), the next turtle, not of this one); the recursion is upward, not a false self-loop. This is the ambient category in which rho's naturality squares commute and the Yoneda evaluations live — the tighter Yoneda realization the maintainer's Directive 2 asks for." .

# The Frame IS the Yoneda point (unary law). Its own representable's Yoneda evaluation
# (prim:yeval_Frame, generated above) yields prim:FrameEncoding = rho(Frame) — the physical
# Frame carrier — so the Frame's self-referential Yoneda evaluation returns the Frame carrier:
# realization = Yoneda evaluation at the representable, closed on the Frame itself.
prim:Frame prim:isYonedaPoint true .
